    <p class="kick">Releases</p>
    <h1 class="h1">What's new in Orbit</h1>
    <p class="doc-lede">Release notes for the Orbit apps on the App Store and for Orbit Server. Newest first.</p>

    <section>
      <h2>Orbit 1.0 — apps for iPhone, Mac, Apple TV and Apple Watch</h2>
      <p class="doc-updated">First release</p>
      <p>Orbit is the native client for your Orbit Server: vinyl pressings, classical hierarchy, several versions per album, and bit-perfect playback on iPhone, Mac, Apple TV and Apple Watch.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Your whole library at home for free: albums, artists, genres, tags, plus the classical and vinyl views, full-quality playback including DSD, lock screen, AirPlay, Apple Watch remote, home-screen widgets.</li>
        <li>Orbit Pro adds remote access over the Orbit Cloud relay, offline downloads, the Apple TV app and CarPlay, Editorial mode, Music Dimensions, exclusive-mode output on Mac, Siri and alternate icons.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Orbit Server 0.2.0</h2>
      <p class="doc-updated">The server the 1.0 apps launch with</p>
      <p>The server ships as a Docker image. Install it, or update an existing server, with the one-line installer, which always fetches the latest release:</p>
      <pre class="o2-code">curl -fsSL https://cloud.orbit.cosmique.io/install.sh | bash</pre>
      <p>Back up before updating: once 0.2.0 has updated its database, an older server will not open it.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Remote playback encodes each track in one continuous pass, so tracks start and seek faster and play without pops over Orbit Cloud.</li>
        <li>Files with no readable tags keep their duration and play remotely.</li>
        <li>Only an administrator can add, change or delete a library, and the web interface asks visitors to sign in before it shows anything.</li>
        <li>Imports ride out a slow MusicBrainz, vinyl and digital copies of an album stay separate, and covers load faster.</li>
        <li>Playlists take several tracks in one step, and smart-playlist rules are fixed.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

